cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SAKE-DT, please cite this software release."
type: software
title: "SAKE-DT: Spectral Autodiff Kernel Expansion for Duhamel Transport"
version: "v0.1-sake-autodiff-dimer"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21793438"
date-released: "2026-08-04"
authors:
  - family-names: Bittner
    given-names: Eric R.
repository-code: "https://github.com/ebitnet65/Duhamel_Transport"
abstract: >
  SAKE-DT is a Spectral Autodiff Kernel Expansion framework for Duhamel
  transport of Liouville-space nonlinear-response pathways. This release
  contains a four-level su(2) x su(2) exciton-dimer model, a JAX/autodiff
  Liouvillian derivative backend, and Duhamel transport expansions through
  third order.
keywords:
  - Duhamel expansion
  - Liouville space
  - autodiff
  - JAX
  - nonlinear spectroscopy
  - two-dimensional spectroscopy
  - exciton dimer
  - pathway transport
  - response functions
